From fdbfb780ca93aaf0adf8cd295f6ab1dcd287d880 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sebastian Matkovich <sebastian.matkovich@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:42:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 156/156] webrender: every shader variant compiles as GLSL ES
 1.00

All 49 GLES shader variants now compile and link in an OpenGL ES 2.0
context (Mesa, ES 2.0 forced, no instancing extensions), next to the
unchanged GL 3 (64) and ES 3 (49) variants.

webrender_build rewrites each line of a Gles2 shader (rewrite_for_gles2,
Gles2Rewriter): texelFetch and TEXEL_FETCH into texel-centre texture2D
lookups with the size from a per-sampler sX_Size uniform it declares,
TEX_SIZE/textureSize/TEX_SIZE_YUV into that uniform, integer samplers
into float ones, integer attributes into float ones (aX_f), integer
varyings into highp float ones that the vertex shader assigns converted
and the fragment shader reads rounded, texture() into texture2D(), mix
with a boolean selector, transpose, inverse and round into wr_* helpers,
and out oFragColor into gl_FragColor; ES 2.0 fragment shaders enable
GL_OES_standard_derivatives for fwidth.

Shared shader changes, the same code for every version: no array
returns or constructors (split composite geometry, border side colours,
component transfer functions), switch case blocks without the extra
braces switch2if left. The 1471 wrench reftests under GL 3 still give
exactly the original results.

wrench compile_shaders: WRENCH_SHADER_DUMP writes every variant's
sources to a directory.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
